From 6bbb3eecfe6143963f9a187581cf52ca8a4275d1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: loonylabs-dev <info@loonylabs.dev>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 22:04:20 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] server: let a cached prompt win on similarity when the
 slot is already a complete prefix

find_best requires a candidate to improve on both f_keep and f_sim. Once the
incumbent is a complete prefix of the new prompt its f_keep is 1.0, and no entry
can beat that: reaching further past the common prefix is exactly what lowers
f_keep. The incumbent is then unbeatable however much more of the prompt an
entry covers.

Measured on a 40k-token prompt with the slot holding a 20k prefix of it and the
cache holding the full 40k:

    slot    f_keep = 1.00000   f_sim = 0.49990
    cache   f_keep = 0.99998   f_sim = 0.99980

The cached entry covers twice as much of the prompt and is rejected over a
0.00002 difference in f_keep.

When f_keep cannot discriminate, let f_sim decide alone. The incumbent is saved
to the cache before a load replaces it, so the trade costs no context. Every
other case keeps its previous outcome, including the f_keep < 0.25 guard against
trashing large prompts and the rejection of entries that cover less.
---
 tools/server/server-task.cpp | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/tools/server/server-task.cpp b/tools/server/server-task.cpp
index 198c5b60c..878e82fa2 100644
--- a/tools/server/server-task.cpp
+++ b/tools/server/server-task.cpp
@@ -1814,7 +1814,14 @@ std::list<server_prompt_cache_state>::iterator server_prompt_cache::find_best(co
             continue;
         }
 
-        if (f_keep_best < f_keep_cur && f_sim_best < f_sim_cur) {
+        // f_keep cannot discriminate once the incumbent is a complete prefix of the new
+        // prompt: it is then 1.0, and any entry that reaches further is necessarily below
+        // it, because reaching further past the common prefix is exactly what lowers
+        // f_keep. Requiring an improvement in both would make such an incumbent
+        // unbeatable however much more of the prompt an entry covers. Let f_sim decide
+        // alone in that case; the incumbent is saved to the cache before it is replaced,
+        // so the trade costs no context
+        if ((f_keep_best >= 1.0f || f_keep_best < f_keep_cur) && f_sim_best < f_sim_cur) {
             f_keep_best = f_keep_cur;
             f_sim_best  = f_sim_cur;
 
-- 
